Three native raylib games

Build in generated9 after installing libgpu, libtinygl and libraylib:

    cd /sys/src/games/raygames
    mk install

Run inside rio with the same VirtIO GPU/VirGL setup as games/raydemo:

    games/arkanoid
    games/asteroids
    games/missile

Arkanoid: Left/Right move the paddle; Space launches the ball.
Asteroids: Left/Right turn, Up accelerates, Down brakes; Space fires.
Missile Commander: point at a target and click button 1, 2 or 3 to fire
from the left, middle or right launcher. Protect the cities and launchers.

All three: P pauses, R restarts, Escape exits. Enter starts another round
after losing. The arena keeps its aspect ratio when the window is resized;
mouse aiming uses the same coordinate transform as drawing.
Paused and game-over windows wait for input or window events instead of
redrawing continuously. The fixed-frame test option keeps timed frames.

No game data need to be downloaded. These are small, single-round games
from the official raylib-games collection, with geometry and a built-in
font, and no audio. They use raylib's classic rendering path on TinyGL/VirGL
and the native Plan 9 C toolchain. See UPSTREAM and LICENSE for provenance.

Options: -n frames exits after a fixed frame count; -s seed selects a
repeatable random sequence; -o file.png captures the last displayed frame.
The original game logic advances once per frame, paced at 60 fps. It slows
down if rendering cannot sustain that rate.

Validation:

    mk test
    games/arkanoid -n 120 -s 1 -o /tmp/arkanoid.png
    games/asteroids -n 120 -s 1 -o /tmp/asteroids.png
    games/missile -n 120 -s 1 -o /tmp/missile.png

The logic tests need no window. They cover launch, brick collision, loss
and restart; meteor splitting; rejected aims, simultaneous detonations,
explosion reuse and expiry, and single scoring of impacts. Interactive checks
exercise real keyboard/mouse input, pause, restart, resizing and PNG capture in rio.
The port has been tested on amd64 with QEMU and VirGL.
